.TH PSMatrixProduct 3 2023-12-03 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSMatrixProduct

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSMatrixProduct\fR(\fIPSMatrix a\fR, \fIPSMatrix b\fR, \fIPSMatrix *result\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opt\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Performs matrix-matrix multiplication between matrix \fIa\fR and matrix \fIb\fR.
.br
Results are stored into matrix pointed by \fIresult\fR. If pointer pointed by \fIresult\fR is \fINULL\fR, a new matrix is automatically allocated by the function itself and its pointer will be stored into \fIresult\fR.
.br
By default, function uses BLAS to compute the result. Anyway, if BLAS support is missing in PsyC build and \fIb\fR only has one dimension, function will try compute results by using \fIPSDotProduct\fR as fallback (for all other cases, it will fail!).
.br
The \fIopt\fR argument can be \fINULL\fR.
.br
You can set matrix transposition using \fItranspose\fR field in the \fIopt\fR argument. In that case, \fItranspose\fR will contain the (1-based) indices of the matrix arguments you want to be transposed:
.br

.RS 4
\[bu] opt->transpose = 1 (transpose matrix \fIa\fR)
.br

\[bu] opt->transpose = 2 (transpose matrix \fIb\fR)
.br

\[bu] opt->transpose = (1 | 2) (transpose both matrix \fIa\fR and \fIb\fR)
.RE
.RE

By default, data in result vector will be overwritten. Anyway, if \fIPS_STORE_MODE_ADD\fR is set as \fIstore_mode\fR into \fIopt\fR, result will be added to data already present in the result vector.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
1 if operation succeeds, 0 if it fails.

.SH SEE ALSO
PSMatrixProductMV(3), PSMatrixProductVM(3)
